Feature: Boiling when it is cheap
  Approval: approved

  A cheap boil tells the kettle to wait until the price is low, so you do not have to watch it.
  You fill the kettle, choose the price you call cheap and ask for a cheap boil. The kettle
  waits until the price reaches your cheap rate, then boils.

  A cheap boil only reacts to a price it can trust. While the feed is unavailable there is no
  price, so the kettle keeps waiting and does not boil on an old one. The same goes for a price
  that arrives while the feed is live: it is checked against your cheap rate as soon as it comes.

  Expectation: Asking for a cheap boil makes the kettle wait
    Given the cheap boil is off
    When the user asks for a cheap boil
    Then the cheap boil is waiting

  Expectation: A cheap price starts the boil
    The kettle starts the moment a live price reaches your cheap rate.
    Given the cheap boil is waiting
    And the price feed is live
    When the price drops to the cheap rate
    Then the cheap boil is boiling

  Expectation: Without a price the kettle keeps waiting
    No price means nothing to compare with your cheap rate, so the kettle stays as it was.
    Given the cheap boil is waiting
    And the price feed is unavailable
    Then the cheap boil is waiting

  Expectation: A delayed price can start the boil
    Approval: proposed
    Unresolved: should an old price start a boil? Boiling sooner may save money, but the real
    price may already have gone back up, and nobody has decided whether the kettle may start
    while the price is in doubt. Until it does, this is proposed and an approved manual leaves
    it out.
    Given the cheap boil is waiting
    And the price feed is delayed
    When the price drops to the cheap rate
    Then the cheap boil is boiling
